            "kind": "VizConfig",
            "spec": {
              "fieldConfig": {
                "defaults": {},
                "overrides": []
              },
              "options": {
                "content": "### Helsinki's trams, metro, trains, ferries and buses, as they move\n\nEvery vehicle of Helsinki Region Transport (HSL) reports where it is **once a second** to a public MQTT broker. Grafana's MQTT datasource subscribes to it, and the positions reach this page through **Grafana Live**, a websocket: nothing polls, and nothing is stored. The map moves the vehicles as their reports arrive and keeps a trail of up to a minute behind each; an arrow is moving, a dot is stopped. Pick the kind of vehicle above.\n\nThe map, the figures and the table on the right all work on the newest 20,000 reports the browser keeps: on a weekday evening, about 50 seconds of trams (HSL sends each tram report four times) or 35 seconds of buses. Trams run from about 5:30 to 1:30 Helsinki time, the metro from 5:30 to 23:30; at night only a few buses and trains report. Buses are many hundreds by day: expect a busier page.\n\nData: HSL high-frequency positioning (HFP v2), `mqtt.hsl.fi`, © Helsinki Region Transport, CC BY 4.0.",
                "mode": "markdown"
              }
            },
            "version": ""
          }
        }
      },
